{"t": 40.428, "n": 39, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the triage note to `plugins/temperspec-tgraph/docs/tasks/i173.triage.md`. That folder sits beside this package's specs, which is where the earlier temperspec tasks keep their notes. I didn't run git, and I didn't write the note to the `docs/tasks/` folder at the repository root.\n\nI opened `task-notes.rule.md` and `documents.rule.md` with the read tool before writing.\n\n- **Acceptance criteria:** all 10 are copied from the task as written.\n- **Gaps:** there are seven. No spec of the package states the review unit, so discovery has to write one.\n  - **G1:** the unit's placement and what the reader is given and never given.\n  - **G2:** the findings document and its model-free check.\n  - **G3:** the single trip back, which step for which kind of finding, and the pause.\n  - **G4:** an existing behaviour. `finalize` in `routing.py` writes the pull request description, but no spec says what it holds.\n  - **G5:** the lane or size bound under which the unit doesn't run.\n  - **G6:** the per-finding record of whether the visit built or refused it (RRN-B14).\n  - **G7:** an update to `overview.spec.md` and `code-join.spec.md` so both show the unit.\n- **Owner decisions:** none. Every gap is marked `Findable`.\n- **Route:** `Deliver: code`, `Route: discovery`.\n- **Covered:** no gap says `Covered by`, so not every gap is covered.\n\nARTIFACT triage_note: plugins/temperspec-tgraph/docs/tasks/i173.triage.md\nARTIFACT gaps: some\nARTIFACT route: discovery\nARTIFACT covered: no", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "4dbd4618-d234-4ece-8c7d-144e2c9e1486"}
